{
	"name": "Tendem: self-driving delegation",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## How this works\n\n**Chat message → Delegate → poll loop.** Waiting costs zero LLM tokens: *Check & Advance* long-polls on Tendem's server (up to 240 × 30s ≈ 2h per pass) and loops on `pending`.\n\nWhen Tendem sends a message, the *Classify Tendem Message* node decides structurally which wire it goes down: a real scoping question flows to the answer agent and back into the loop; a message that already IS the answer (Tendem answers trivial briefs for free in the chat) or needs nothing flows straight to *Deliver Result* — it has no wire to Reply, so nothing gets sent back.\n\n**Money:** quotes route to *Approve*, whose policy ships as **Never** — it reports the quote and charges nothing. Open it and pick *Under Max Price* (set a cap) or *From Decision Field* (wire a Slack/form approval) when you're ready to let it spend.\n\nFiles attached via the chat **paperclip** upload to the task automatically (node 0.2.3+).\n\n**After import:** select your **Tendem API** credential on the 4 Tendem Expert nodes and your **OpenRouter** credential on the model node. Replace *Deliver Result* with Slack/email/whatever.",
				"height": 420,
				"width": 420
			},
			"id": "note-1",
			"name": "Sticky Note",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-560,
				-140
			]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"options": {
					"allowFileUploads": true
				}
			},
